KG42.register("clusters-05ac9a732be386067935606b",{"id":"02-dlmp::v142-d-CL001","paper":"02-dlmp","label":"Day-ahead distribution welfare clearing and DLMP formation","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL001","label":"Day-ahead distribution welfare clearing and DLMP formation","market_meaning":"The DSO obtains day-ahead system prices and forecasts demand, performs social-welfare clearing using demand value, electricity supply costs, and network and charging feasibility conditions, and produces nodal allocations and DLMPs for the following day. The price decomposition is interpreted under the RBTS reference-node simplification and interiority conditions for conventional demand; the existing references are not yet sufficient to complete the full optimization and pricing derivation.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["clearing","coordination","pricing"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"All chains belong to the same distribution market mechanism, with explicit dependencies among information preparation, welfare optimization, feasibility, and price outputs. The price decompositions in R001 and R006 are read together only within the common scope in which the PTDF at the RBTS generation node is zero and constraint (7) is nonbinding; the general welfare objective and the linear demand and elasticity values in the case retain their respective scopes of applicability.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Taking the DSO's day-ahead constrained optimization and its price outputs as the decision boundary, this cluster combines input preparation, the objective, the feasible set, and pricing. Autonomous energy purchasing by aggregators after price publication has independent inputs and decisions and is primarily assigned to a separate cluster; the discussion of decentralized implementation in this cluster serves as shared support for that cluster.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides feasibility conditions for local allocation and an equilibrium interpretation of clearing prices, jointly defining central clearing with the welfare objective."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the DSO welfare objective, supply costs, and the treatment of EV utility, constituting the core optimization decision for which this cluster is responsible."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"interface","rationale":"Provides procedures for obtaining system prices and forecasting demand, whose outputs are explicitly used for welfare calculation and DLMP formation."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the relationship through which welfare clearing produces DLMP and the price decomposition with its accompanying conditions, constituting this cluster's price outputs."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-p-LMP","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E37","v141-b-g01-E09"],"rationale":"The day-ahead system LMP obtained by the DSO corresponds to the exogenous supply-price input in the welfare objective. R003 retains only procedural objects; this interface does not invent additional parameters for it."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E37"],"rationale":"Step 3 explicitly uses forecast demand and accounts for network topology to calculate DLMP, supporting an information dependency between forecasting and pricing; this mapping is based on the actual use of inputs, rather than step numbering."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C006","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C007","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C008","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C009"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E13"],"rationale":"The source explicitly places welfare objective (1) subject to constraints (2)-(9). The objective in R002 and the feasibility conditions already included in R001 jointly describe the same optimization problem, but this does not establish that all constraints are explicitly present in C."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R006::x::x_P_DLMP"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E01","v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g01-E22"],"rationale":"The source explicitly attributes the next day's DLMP to the results of the DSO's constrained welfare optimization, so the objective decision and price outputs should be assembled together; this relationship does not supply the missing KKT derivation."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L05","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E22"],"rationale":"The same (33) and its congestion-markup definition are written together in R001 and separately in R006. They are read together as a composite formulation only under the shared RBTS simplification and interior-point conditions; the combined object cannot be equated individually with each constituent object, nor are additional independent rules counted."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-O01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R003::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R006::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R003::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g01-E37"],"rationale":"These existing nodes all refer to the DSO that obtains inputs, performs welfare optimization, and calculates prices within the same mechanism; the representative is selected solely for display, and all original references are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-O02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::clearing.social_welfare","v141-c-R006::V::clearing.social_welfare"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R002::V::clearing.social_welfare","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E01","v141-b-g01-E08"],"rationale":"Both occurrences refer to the same DSO welfare-clearing function that produces the next day's DLMP and may share a display representative."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-O03","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E26"],"rationale":"Both occurrences refer to the nodal DLMP pricing function of this distribution market; node identity does not remove the conditions accompanying each formula."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-O04","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R002::V::coordination.price_signal"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R001::V::coordination.price_signal","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g01-E35"],"rationale":"Both occurrences refer to the coordination function that implements decentralized responses through DLMP publication; this display identity does not demonstrate that the mathematical conditions for decentralized implementation are complete."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-O05","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-002","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-c"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E13"],"rationale":"Both objects represent conventional demand at the same node and in the same period within the same DSO problem, used respectively for nodal balance and welfare valuation; their respective bindings and local roles are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-O06","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-001","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-x"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E15"],"rationale":"Within the scope of central optimization, the two objects correspond to the same nodal charging quantity, carrying feasibility conditions and cost valuation, respectively. This association does not establish that an arbitrary aggregator response equals the central optimal quantity."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-O07","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-006","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-p-LMP","v141-c-R006::theta::theta_P_LMP"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E37"],"rationale":"The system LMP for the same supply node and period serves respectively as an input to cost valuation, clearing interpretation, and price decomposition; only identity is linked, without rewriting local parameters."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-O08","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-001","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-p-E"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E13"],"rationale":"Both objects correspond to the time-varying upper bound on charging energy in central clearing constraint (8); identity is based on the constraint and its physical meaning, rather than on the symbol alone."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-O09","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-007","v141-c-R006::theta::theta_D_li"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E22"],"rationale":"Within the same network and the corresponding demand-node scope, both objects are line-to-node PTDFs. R001's broader network indexing and R006's pricing use are still retained separately."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G01","category":"math_incomplete","description":"Although R001 and R002 list constraint families, the existing mathematical objects do not explicitly cover (3), (4), (5), (7), or the complete DSO KKT system. In particular, the closure relations between supply quantities and network balance, and between line capacities and line dual variables, cannot be recovered solely from the objective and price decomposition.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-q","v141-c-R006::x::x_lambda_plus","v141-c-R006::x::x_lambda_minus"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g01-E18"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Have the upstream stage check and complete the required constraints, objects, and bindings in a subsequent C version, or explicitly limit the assembly to references to the objective and partial feasibility conditions; D keeps the objects from this round unchanged."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G02","category":"scope_conflict","description":"R001-C004 explicitly states only that the nonnegativity constraint on conventional demand is nonbinding, whereas R006-C003 additionally specifies that the PTDF at the RBTS generation node is zero. Their applicability conditions have not yet been fully aligned in the frozen records.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C004","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E19","v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g01-E22"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually confirm the common scope of applicability, and have the upstream stage clarify whether the pricing formulation in R001 inherits the RBTS reference-node condition; the current connection between alternative formulations is interpreted only under the shared conditions."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G03","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The cost terms on the two sides of the equality in (10) in E15 are inconsistent, so this cannot confirm a decomposition that is identically equal to the complete objective. R002-C004 retains only the three-term right-hand side and cannot be directly declared a verified identical expression to R002-C001.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E15"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Recheck (10) in the source and its relationship to supply balance before deciding how the objective representations correspond; retain the existing right-hand-side expression and the uncertainty in the original source."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G04","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The line set, some indices, and the EV and demand dual quantities lack explicit C objects or complete bindings. E13 already explains the meaning of driving energy, so it can no longer be described as wholly undefined, but its units, time step, and aggregation basis remain insufficiently specified; the formulations in terms of power and energy by period also require checking.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-005","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-003","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-p-P","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g01-E25"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Have the upstream stage further check symbol definitions, dimensions, period conventions, and the classification of equilibrium quantities, and determine the cross-chain binding approach; shared references cannot be treated as newly added C declarations."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G05","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The omission of EV utility in R002 depends on intraday energy requirements being met. The SOC accumulation in R001-C009 includes only charging before the current period, and the frozen objects do not explicitly specify end-of-day closure or how charging in the final period satisfies this prerequisite. The existing material is insufficient to independently verify this condition.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C009","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E14"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the planning-horizon boundaries, SOC timing, and conditions for meeting intraday requirements; if the source provides a separate terminal convention, have the upstream stage explicitly include it. Otherwise, retain the conditional gap without independently inventing constraints."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G06","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The congestion markup is already represented by existing price objects and expressions, but the proposal for a dedicated node remains unapproved; this assembly does not turn it into a new graph node.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R006::x::x_varphi","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g01-E22"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-prop-congestion-markup"],"required_work":"Manually decide whether a separate ontology node for the congestion markup is needed; continue using frozen-object references until that decision is made."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G07","category":"unverified_source","description":"All B materials used by this cluster retain unverified status and are eligible for citation only under the policy for experimental candidate support. The B source audit, C2 independent review, and Agent E have not been run; the assembly does not signify independent confirmation of the transcriptions or scientific derivations.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E25","v141-b-g01-E37"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"For manual, item-by-item checking of the sources, formulas, and this cluster's boundaries; if scientific confirmation is subsequently needed, source and mathematical verification should be completed separately."}]},"rule_refs":["02-dlmp::v141-c-R001","02-dlmp::v141-c-R002","02-dlmp::v141-c-R003","02-dlmp::v141-c-R006"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-276b46f772c03e0a","COMP-5e870d267afec9a0","COMP-80212c4bda48caf5","COMP-ab3d11c48c98c7be","COMP-fe1ce5f5844f5ec1"]});
